{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Create a national register for supply teaching staff and cap agency profits",
        "additional_details": "We demand a national register helping checked supply teaching staff to work directly with schools, and strict limits on teaching agency fees and profits.\r\n \r\nAgencies often take a large share of the money schools pay for supply staff. This can mean lower pay for staff, higher costs for schools, and less money for pupils and facilities.\r\n\r\nRegistered staff should list their qualifications, experience, availability, and safeguarding clearance so schools can book them directly. Public money should support children\u2019s education, not excessive recruitment profits.\r\n",
        "background": "We demand that the Government create a national register helping suitably checked supply teaching staff to work directly with schools, and introduce strict legal limits on the fees, commissions, and profit margins charged by teaching agencies.",
